# A fresh census of youtube's full rebuilds (r105, 380 binary): its four
# <iframe> batches -- the iframe now built alone (378) and past the
# structural check (380) -- declined on patch 198's "sibling combinator
# may restyle on insert/remove": youtube's sheets are in patch 186's
# conservative state (a pseudo-class in a sibling rule's left compound),
# for which html_rl_block_sibling_risk declines every change outright.
#
# A + / ~ rule restyles the element AFTER its left compound's element. A
# change at the parent's tail -- elements appended with nothing after them
# but tags that never have a box, the last block removed, a box-less
# removal whose recorded place (380) is the end -- moves no existing
# sibling's match; the moved elements are built afresh.
#  - html_rl_block_sibling_risk gains a tail mode: no per-element
#    combinator analysis, no conservative-sheet decline. The parent's
#    :empty flipping still counts (a conservative sheet declines on a
#    flip: its :empty list cannot be trusted). :has() is not checked: this
#    libcss parses it and never matches it (patch 328,
#    selector_never_matches_part), as patch 369 relies on; if :has()
#    matching is ever added, this must decline on it (youtube's sheets
#    name :has()).
#  - html_rl_block_change uses it for a child-list mark on this parent
#    whose added elements are followed only by box-less tags
#    (html_rl_at_tail) and whose removed blocks were the last; the 378
#    no-op for an appendChild (the node went last) or a removal placed at
#    the end. html_reconvert_local_childlist now also carries whether the
#    mark was an appendChild (macos9_reconvert.c).
#
# Result on a 2500-paragraph sim page with a conservative sibling sheet:
# an <iframe> appended to <body> 123 -> 32 ms; a block appended to a list
# 117 -> 26 ms. On youtube the four iframe blocks are built locally.
#
